{#- Role: ask the MLLM for every instance of the dataset's classes, as JSON boxes.
    Variables: class_names (list of str); descriptions (dict name -> text, few-shot only,
    may be empty); instructions (str, few-shot only, may be empty).
    Expected output: JSON list of {"bbox_2d": [x1, y1, x2, y2], "label": <class name>},
    coordinates in the model's own format (Qwen3-VL: relative, 0-1000); the wrapper converts.
    The first sentence is the Qwen3-VL report's ODinW prompt (App. B.5, p37). -#}
Locate every instance that belongs to the following categories: '{{ class_names | join(", ") }}'. Report bbox coordinates in JSON format.
{%- if descriptions %}

Category descriptions:
{%- for name, text in descriptions.items() %}
- {{ name }}: {{ text }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if instructions %}

Annotation instructions:
{{ instructions }}
{%- endif %}
Use exactly the category names above as "label".
